## Issue / fix: feat: preserve change markers when combining --diff with --plain

## Description
## Summary

When `--plain` is set (via CLI or config file), `--diff` output loses all visual markers - no `~`/`+`/`-` change indicators and no `Snip` separators between hunks. The diff line filtering still works (only changed regions are shown), but the output is indistinguishable from plain text.

The root cause is `forced_style_components()` which returns early with only `StyleComponent::Plain` (resolving to an empty decoration set) before `--style` arguments can be parsed. The user's workaround of adding `--style=full` also fails because forced components take priority.

### Fix

When `--plain` is set AND `--diff` is also active, automatically include `Changes` and `Snip` style components. This preserves the `--plain` intent (no grid, no header, no line numbers) while keeping diff output readable.

**Note:** This is a behavior change. I'd welcome feedback on whether this automatic approach is preferred, or if an alternative like a warning message or a new dedicated style component would be better.

## Test plan

- [ ] `bat --diff --plain file.c` shows change markers and snip separators
- [ ] `bat --plain file.c` (without --diff) behavior is unchanged
- [ ] `bat --diff file.c` (without --plain) behavior is unchanged
- [ ] Works when `--plain` is set via `BAT_CONFIG_FILE`
- [ ] `cargo test` passes
- [ ] `cargo clippy` clean

