## Issue / fix: Use all CPUs during an import dump

## Description
# Pull Request

## Related issue
Fixes #5514 

## What does this PR do?
Creates a temporary thread pool using all CPUs to index a dump on startup if `max_indexing_threads` not configured.
- Updates `MaxThreads(usize)` to `MaxThreads(Option<usize>)` as in `MaxMemory`. Without an option somewhere there is no way to distinguish a value provided by the user from Meili's default, stopping us from expressing conditional logic at index time
- Moves the default behaviour of using 1/2 of the cpu threads from `MaxThreads::default()` to `IndexerConfig::try_from()` 
- Changes `thread_pool` from `Option<ThreadPoolNoAbort>` to `ThreadPoolNoAbort`
- Simplifies tests


