## Issue / fix: Fix gradients in LinearRGB, CMYK and Luma spaces for SVG and PDF export

## Description
Fixes #8139

Changes:
- Use sRGB instead of LinearRgb when determining the intermediate stops, as sRGB is the native color space used by SVG and PDF (this only concerns finding the intermediate stop positions, stop colors always use the gradient space, see below) a25282a6
- Enable the code path which generates intermediate stops in PDF also for LinearRGB. 765115b8
- Convert all stop colors to the target space before writing them to SVG/PDF. This fixes an issue in Luma interpolation, where the first and last stop would be emitted as-is, resulting in colorful edges for the grayscale gradient. 06b236a6
- For PDF export, encode colors in the target space where possible (avoids conversion of CMYK and Luma colors to RGB). 420c4620
- In `sample_stops` make sure the first stop is also converted to the mixing space. This fixes the yellow slice at the start of the Luma gradient not being grayscale in PNG export c02bcfd5
- Add a test containing all the color spaces to replace the dedicated tests for HSV, HSL, Oklch and OKlab. The test suite missed LinearRGB, CMYK and Luma (the ones which regressed), so having a test with all spaces should prevent future regressions 8551fc333fa75e407203bdcb0b1fa88040054beb d6886c1e ff859459
 
