## Issue / fix: Add divider element

## Description
This PR implements the `divider` element based on the design outlined by @laurmaedje in #7616. It continues the work started by @LegNeato

The divider is an empty element without its own styling. It has a default show rule that specifies its behavior.

Default behavior:
- 2 em spacing around
- Renders as 0.05em line
- HTML export to `<hr>`

By default, it basically behaves as:
```typst
#show divider: set block(spacing: 2em)
#show divider: line(length: 100%, stroke: 0.05em)
```

Users can customize it with their own show rules, for example:
```typst
#show divider: block(spacing: 1em)[
	#line(length: 80%, stroke: 2pt + blue)
]
```

Closes #5318

