## Description
<!-- Describe your changes in detail -->
<img width="1185" height="133" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2e7adb86-6af7-4ed9-8bdf-9611e9797f0c" />

Rust 1.94 gives warnings regarding the size of the `Err` variant. The primary intent for this lint, (as mentioned in the [PR](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust-clippy/pull/9373) that introduced it) is to flag `Err` variants larger than `Ok` variant. However in the case of `response` in `RouterData`, the `Ok` field itself is quite big. Also, this is not a library error that would then be wrapped inside another error, so the problem of cascading error size is also not there. Boxing the `ErrorResponse` is a very significant change, affecting multiple files, with little apparent benefit. So, replaced the closures with `match` statements to silence the warnings for now

- Converted `map_or_else` closures into match statements to workaround the warning with minimal changes

