## Issue / fix: fix(go): prevent double-counted failures when test-level fail also triggers package-level fail (#958)

## Description
## Summary

Fixes #958

- `go test -json` always emits a trailing package-level `{"action":"fail"}` after each test-level failure (no `Test` field). The previous code counted both events, so a run with 1 failing test showed **"2 failed"** in the summary header.
- The package also appeared twice in the output: once as a `[FAIL]` block and again in the per-package test results section.
- Fix: `total_pkg_fail` now only includes packages where `package_failed=true` **and** there are no individual test- or build-level failures — i.e. pure package-level failures (timeouts, signals, panics). The `[FAIL]` display section skips packages that already have test-level results below.

