## Issue / fix: detect lexer-stage errors at highlighting

## Description
<!--
Thank you for improving Nushell!
Please, read our contributing guide: https://github.com/nushell/nushell/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md
-->
## Description

Fixes #17916.

The underlying issue is that some code is already rejected at the lexer stage: `out>|`, `&&` etc. are all invalid tokens that are rejected by the lexer. In `nu_parser::lex_item` we emit an error, but still tokenize and persist them - specifically, we tokenize as `TokenContents::Item`.So, by the time the lite-parser starts, the information about this invalidity is lost.

That's a problem for nu-highlight, which needs to highlight the problem code as garbage. For internal commands we still get error highlighting because we go through `parse_value` to validate shape, and later check the shape during highlighting. For externals we don't (also for some other code, see tests).

My first attempt was threading the invalid tokens all the way to nu-highlight. This turned up to be messy. Instead we do the following: during highlighting, we lex again and update the nu-highlight garbage detection with errors found from the lexing.

## Release notes summary - What our users need to know
<!--
This section will be included as part of our release notes. See the contributing guide for more details.
Please include only details relevant for users here. Motivation and technical details can be added above or below this section.
-->

Some code that was already known to be invalid early-on, will now be highlight

